From 9fc74d06b1b29ac28a85caf3911c5ee2b62275ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:08:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native query pool and standalone Beast
 HTTP/WebSocket listener

Add chronik_native_transport, which serves the Router and WebSocket
handlers on -chronikbind without Rust's axum/tokio:

- QueryPool: a fixed thread pool on which every request handler runs.
  AsyncHandle(pool, router, request, token) completes on the caller's Asio
  executor (callback or use_awaitable), so io threads never block; the
  in-process /chronik bridge reuses it.
- BeastListener: Boost.Beast HTTP/1.1 with keep-alive on each bind address,
  its own io_context with 2 threads, the 2 MB request body limit (413 by
  Content-Length or chunked body), no TLS, and the bind error text of the
  Rust server.
- WebSocket on /ws: a strand per session, non-blocking SendBinary, a
  20,000-byte message limit, Pong replies, a Ping with payload
  "Bitcoin ABC Chronik Indexer" after the idle interval (45 s, 5 s on
  regtest), text frames passed to the handler. Handler callbacks run one at
  a time per session on the query pool.

The tests run a real listener on 127.0.0.1:0 and exercise GET, HEAD,
POST, OPTIONS, 404/405/413, CORS, keep-alive, two binds, address-in-use,
and WebSocket echo, close, ping/pong and oversized messages.

Tier: eCash
